      "Language": "rus",
      "Abstract": {"AbstractText": "Repeated pharmacodynamic studies of more than 30 drugs with hypotensive, antianginal and antiarrhythmic effects were performed in over 1,200 patients suffering from cardiovascular diseases, predominantly ischemic heart disease and hypertensive disease. The result of the work was optimization of the drug dosage regimen during course treatment; real diagnostic possibilities of functional research methods were revealed."},
